"type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477c"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4730"], "question": {"text": "Heat treatment of muscular pain involves radiation of wavelength of about $900 \\mathrm{nm}$. Which spectral line of $\\mathrm{H}$ atom is suitable for this purpose? $\\left[\\mathrm{R}_{\\mathrm{H}}=1 \\times 10^{5} \\mathrm{~cm}^{-1} \\cdot \\mathrm{h}=6.6 \\times 10^{-34} \\mathrm{Js}, \\mathrm{c}=3 \\times 10^{8} \\mathrm{~ms}^{-1}\\right]$"}, "options": [{"id": "2ec7b9", "text": "Paschen, $\\infty \\rightarrow 3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f474"}, {"id": "941c96", "text": "Paschen, $5 \\rightarrow 3$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f475"}, {"id": "ccd65d", "text": "Balmer, $\\infty \\rightarrow 2$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f476"}, {"id": "a0db0f", "text": "Lyman, $\\infty \\rightarrow 1$", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f477"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f478", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b78"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5671"], "question": {"text": "If \\(\\mathrm{a}_0\\) is denoted as the Bohr radius of hydrogen atom, then what is the de-Broglie wavelength \\((\\lambda)\\) of the electron present in the second orbit of hydrogen atom? [n : any integer]"}, "options": [{"id": "75b4b7", "text": "\\(\\frac{8 \\pi a_0}{n}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f479"}, {"id": "55783d", "text": "\\(\\frac{2 a_0}{n \\pi}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f47a"}, {"id": "473ce8", "text": "\\(\\frac{4 \\mathrm{n}}{\\pi \\mathrm{a}_0}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f47b"}, {"id": "1c7d73", "text": "\\(\\frac{4 \\pi a_0}{n}\\)", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f47c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f47d", "type": "singleCorrect", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e5671c499d1e49588f8801"], "concepts": ["60e5671a499d1e49588f87da"], "question": {"text": "<p>Arrange the following orbitals in decreasing order of energy.</p><p>A.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />B.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />C.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />D.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>The correct option for the order is:</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "ff0a9c", "text": "D &gt; B &gt; C &gt; A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f47e"}, {"id": "dd8a6d", "text": "B &gt; D &gt; C &gt; A", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f47f"}, {"id": "debfb0", "text": "A &gt; C &gt; B &gt; D", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f480"}, {"id": "f901a5", "text": "D &gt; B &gt; A &gt; C", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f481"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283e223cf4b3ad8f125e6", "title": "JEE Single Correct", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:15.785Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 20, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:05.867Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:05.867Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 0, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4fc"}, {"sectionId": {"_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4f9", "title": "Chemistry Numerical", "sectionType": "normal", "subject": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "questions": [{"_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b477c"], "concepts": ["60e2fb9d66f9ce3f243b52c0"], "question": {"text": "Wavenumber for a radiation having \\(5800 Ã…\\) wavelength is \\(x \\times 10 \\mathrm{~cm}^{-1}\\). The value of \\(x\\) is ________ (Integer answer)"}, "options": [{"id": "49b91a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b1"}, {"id": "974621", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b2"}, {"id": "801d6a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b3"}, {"id": "bb6008", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb2066f9ce3f243b4b78"], "concepts": ["60e2fbdc66f9ce3f243b5671"], "question": {"text": "The wavelength of an electron and a neutron will become equal when the velocity of the electron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> times the velocity of neutron. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&nbsp;is____(the nearest integer)(Mass of electron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and mass of neutron is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math>)"}, "options": [{"id": "d9ae7c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b6"}, {"id": "28d0a3", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b7"}, {"id": "07051a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b8"}, {"id": "9f7d7e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4b9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4ba", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b478d"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b4746"], "question": {"text": "For a metal ion, the calculated magnetic moment is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>BM</mi></math>. This metal ion has _______ number of unpaired electrons"}, "options": [{"id": "ab9528", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4bb"}, {"id": "8b7136", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4bc"}, {"id": "1bca0e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4bd"}, {"id": "2aed55", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4be"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4bf", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["60e2fb5766f9ce3f243b4f49"], "concepts": ["60e2fad966f9ce3f243b471c"], "question": {"text": "<p>The kinetic energy of an electron in the second Bohr orbit of a hydrogen atom is equal to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi>ma</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is (<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math> is radius of Bohr&#39;s orbit)</p><p>(Nearest integer)</p><p>[Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#960;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "8f3f92", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4c0"}, {"id": "b29755", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4c1"}, {"id": "5ec380", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4c2"}, {"id": "1e62dd", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4c3"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4c4", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0dfb1"], "topics": ["6162fb5a6ed13040ec84de88"], "concepts": ["62516bc346c70d030bd3f0a0"], "question": {"text": "<p>Electrons in a cathode ray tube have been emitted with a velocity of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1000</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>ms</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The number of following statements which is/are true about the emitted radiation is</p><p>Given :&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>34</mn></mrow></msup><mi>Js</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>31</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math></p><p>(A ) The deBroglie wavelength of the electron emitted is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>666</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>67</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>nm</mi></math></p><p>(B ) The characteristic of electrons emitted depend upon the material of the electrodes of the cathode ray tube.</p><p>(C) The cathode rays start from cathode and move towards anode.</p><p>(D ) The nature of the emitted electrons depends on the nature of the gas present in cathode ray tube..</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "1b64df", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4c5"}, {"id": "8e4194", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4c6"}, {"id": "2d723c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4c7"}, {"id": "8a0fe0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4c8"}], "questionLabels": []}], "markingScheme": {"_id": "608283c623cf4b3ad8f125e5", "title": "JEE Numerical", "correctAttempt": 4, "incorrectAttempt": -1, "createdAt": "2021-04-09T08:45:27.797Z", "updatedAt": "2021-07-05T05:39:27.056Z", "__v": 0, "updated_by": "6042252509c5bf34e8a2f178"}, "maximumAttemptLimit": 5, "linkedQuestions": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:05.972Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-14T14:30:05.972Z", "__v": 0}, "position": 1, "_id": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f4fd"}], "bonusSections": [], "packDetails": [], "paidFeatures": [], "tags": [], "timeRestrictionSlots": [], "createdAt": "2026-04-14T11:16:02.852Z", "updatedAt": "2026-04-17T04:58:02.309Z", "testType": "PYQs as Chapter Tests", "isResumeBufferAllowed": true, "enableAccessibility": true, "maxAttemptableQuestion": 25, "analysisVideoThumbnail": "", "analysisVideoThumbnailDark": "", "shortTitle": "", "subjectDetails": [{"subjectId": "607018ee404ae53194e73d91", "title": "Chemistry", "shortName": "Chem"}], "testTimerType": "mm", "isMarkForReviewAvailable": true}, "temporaryTestDetail": {"_id": "6a4a1e979cbf3c651304d841", "testId": "69de21f27e39d99b57bc5b28", "userId": "6914cc9c4d7566258ee3a8fd", "startedAt": "2026-07-05T09:06:31.963Z", "lastAttemptedSection": null, "totalTimeLeft": 37, "bonusAttempt": false, "sections": [{"sectionId": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f488", "questions": [{"questionId": "69de4f6dc677dc36a891f41e", "markedOptions": [], "inputValue": null, "timeTaken": 0, "timeLeftWhenAttempted": null, "status": "notVisited", "_id": "6a4a1e979